            <p><strong><font color="#1a62a9" size="3" face="Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">E-Mail 
              Marketing</font></strong></p>
            <p><br>
              Don't neglect e-mail as an important way to bring people to your 
              website. Just don't spam. That is, don't send bulk unsolicited e-mails 
              without permission to people with whom you have no relationship.</p>
            <p> <strong>Publish an E-Mail Newsletter.</strong> While it's a big 
              commitment in time, publishing a monthly or bi-monthly e-mail newsletter 
              (&quot;ezine&quot;) is one of the very best ways to keep in touch 
              with your prospects, generate trust, develop brand awareness, and 
              build future business. It also helps you collect e-mail addresses 
              from those who become a member of your site but aren't yet ready 
              to make a purchase. You can distribute your newsletter using group 
              email feature of your website.</p>
            <p><strong>Send Offers to Your Visitors and Customers.</strong> Your 
              own list of customers and site members who have given you permission 
              to contact them will be your most productive list. Send offers, 
              coupon specials, product updates, etc. Personalizing the subject 
              line and the message will increase the results.</p>
            <p><strong>Spam is in the eye of the beholder.</strong> If you have 
              permission to send the newsletter to members, your recipients aren't 
              likely to view you as a spammer. But Internet email systems might 
              think you're a spammer if you send out large number of e-mails within 
              short period of time. Or, more likely, they may just blacklist your 
              e-mail addresses and filter out your email before reach the recipient. 
              You probably won't get anyone to tell you what the current limit 
              of outgoing e-mails is -- you'll need to set your limits. From time 
              to time an ISP (Internet service Providers) may change how many 
              e-mails it allows in any given time period, so prepare to be flexible. 
              We are using Group e-mail feature to sent out bulk emails. Group 
              email feature has programmed to send out 5 e-mails at a time. Wait 
              for 1 hour before sending the next &quot;pulse&quot; of e-mails. 
              If you are sending same email to more than five recipients, look 
              at the e-mail report and re-send e-mails to the failures. If you 
              do it correctly, your email will be in the recipient's inbox - not 
              in the junk email folder. </p>
